A||||5||82-T/A||MOVED THE FIERO!!!||||1||
Z||000000||82-T/A||11-27-2000||11:09 AM||||Well, in case you all were interested. I moved my 1984 Fiero 2m4 SE from where it was to my parents new house. It was a 10 mile drive. I haven't actually driven the car in over 8 months, and I don't remember it driving that well before I put it in storage. Anyway, I spend about $40 bucks on it Saturday afternoon. New fuel filter, changed the oil, octane booster, filled up all the tires, checked everything to make sure it was ok.<P>I was REALLY worried, and expecting the absolute worst.. I had TWO fire extinguishers with me in the car, a large bottle of water (in case the fire extinguishers didn't work), I had rope to tow the car with... I was extra careful. <P>But.. much to my surprise... the car drove perfect, I took it on the highway at about 65 miles an hour and just cruised all the way till the exit I was supposed to go off. <P>I had my dad follow behind me because I had expired tags. But I was really impressed. I was almost sure it would catch fire or something.. I mean, sitting for soo long.<P>Anyway, I'm going to get started on re-doing the suspension next weekend if I can. The car looks like it rolled off the showroom floor, inside and out.. except the suspension and motor are a little tired. The suspension more so than the engine.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||11-27-2000||01:29 PM||||My current fiero had been sitting for 2 years before I picked it up. Unfortunatly, the previous owner wasn't as thoughtful as you when she started it up to see if it would still run and well, it was not too happy about that. But she went 45 miles threw the countryside and up I-95 with out so much as a hiccup, just a quiet knock. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||82-T/A||11-27-2000||03:07 PM||||Poor Fiero..... <P>Mine needs a bit of work... it runs great... but I think I'll still rebuild the motor.<P>It could definately use the Fiero Store's 1984 Performance Rebuild kit.<P>I've got that planned, all new suspension bushings.. repainting all the suspension parts.. checking everything for rust... re-tapping all old bolts.. and painting the entire exhaust system. Also all new engine mounts and bearings.<P>Should run pretty sweet when I'm done. I expect it will be just about what a V6 Fiero will run. But it will get better gas mileage. and still be fairly original.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||11-27-2000||09:11 PM||||Painting the exhaust? Hmmm, ok. Well, Im glad to here she ran good. Fix her up nice! Gotta keep as many Fieros on the road as possible!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000004||Smokey||11-27-2000||09:15 PM||||Speaking of an 84 4cylinder running beside a V6...what happened to SloPonti?||||reg||1
Z||000005||82-T/A||11-27-2000||10:07 PM||||Yeah, I was going to paint the exhaust black. Just like the rest of the underside of the Fiero.<P>I've got the Ocelot twin tip exhaust tip on it.<P>Only one side.. it's like the best OEM looking replacement for the 4 cyl exhaust.<P>I'll post pics when I've got them.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
